# Copy to `.deploy.env` (gitignored) to deploy your OWN instance. `pnpm deploy`
# (scripts/deploy.sh) injects these into the built worker config so the
# committed wrangler.json stays generic — no account-specific values in git.

# Required: your D1 database id (`wrangler d1 create openrostrum` prints it).
# Quote values — the script sources this file, so spaces and <> need quotes.
CF_D1_DATABASE_ID="your-d1-database-id"

# Optional: override the committed defaults for your deployment.
# EMAIL_FROM="OpenRostrum <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
# APP_ENV="production"

# --- GitHub Actions: per-PR previews ---
# Repo secrets (same token as production deploy, plus create/delete):
#   CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
#   CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
# Token permissions the preview job needs on that account:
#   Account / Workers Scripts: Edit
#   Account / D1: Edit
#   Account / Workers R2 Storage: Edit
#   Account / Workers AI: Read (the committed AI binding is remote)
# Isolation is enforced by scripts/preview/, not by Cloudflare resource ACLs.
# A same-repo PR's build step runs with this token; do not make `preview` a
# required check. Preview does NOT use CF_D1_DATABASE_ID, RESEND_API_KEY,
# APP_ORIGIN, UNSUBSCRIBE_SECRET, or Airtable secrets. Missing Cloudflare
# secrets skip the job green; they do not fail `quality`.
# The preview job also needs pull-requests: write (GITHUB_TOKEN) to upsert
# the workers.dev comment.
